  "id": "attractor-dynamics",
  "term": "attractor dynamics",
  "definition": "Attractor dynamics refers to the tendency of a changing system to be pulled toward some states and away from others over time. In plain language, it describes repeated patterns that persist despite ongoing disturbances, with the most likely states showing relative stability.",
